==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Kaijin Doge]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*2 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Camelle]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**10 [[Kaijin Doge]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
**2 [[Malizabeth]]s spawn, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
**2 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Try to stall the Gabriels and Kaijin Doges that spawn at the start with a single [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] and some meatshields while you build up your wallet. Once your King Dragon Cat kills everything and makes its way to the enemy base, wait until Malizabeth goes in front of Camelle, then summon [[Scarf Cat (Special Cat)|Red Cat]] as well as [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cats]]/King Dragon Cats. Time [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] to kill Angelic Gory almost instantly once he spawns. As soon as both frontliners die, use [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] to hopefully knock back Camelle. Repeat the process for the second Evilzabeth/Angelic Gory wave. Unfortunately, Bahamut is not guaranteed to survive the first encounter, so use [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|True Valkyrie Cat]] to pick up the slack if applicable.

